    "number": 23,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "text": "The LORD Is My Shepherd"
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "text": "A Psalm of David.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 17,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "text": "The LORD is my shepherd;\nI shall not want.",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "noteId": 50,
            "offset": 24,
            "text": "See Revelation 7:17.",
            "caller": "+"
          }
        ],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 24,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 42,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "text": "He makes me lie down in green pastures;\nHe leads me beside quiet waters.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 39,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 72,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "text": "He restores my soul;\nHe guides me in the paths of righteousness\nfor the sake of His name.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 20,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 21,
            "end": 63,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 64,
            "end": 89,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "text": "Even though I walk through the valley of the shadow of death,\nI will fear no evil,\nfor You are with me;\nYour rod and Your staff, they comfort me.",
        "footnotes": [
          {
            "noteId": 51,
            "offset": 61,
            "text": "Or the valley of deep darkness",
            "caller": "+"
          }
        ],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 61,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 62,
            "end": 82,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 103,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 104,
            "end": 145,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "line_break"
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "text": "You prepare a table before me\nin the presence of my enemies.\nYou anoint my head with oil;\nmy cup overflows.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 29,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 30,
            "end": 60,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 89,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 107,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "text": "Surely goodness and mercy will follow me\nall the days of my life,\nand I will dwell in the house of the LORD\nforever.",
        "footnotes": [],
        "poem": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 40,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 65,
            "level": 2
          },
          {
            "start": 66,
            "end": 107,
            "level": 1
          },
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 116,
            "level": 2
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": []
  },
